# Candidate (UNRESOLVED) — Credentialed CORS reflection on sso.ui.com

**Status:** Not confirmed — no impact demonstrated.
**Severity if exploitable:** unknown.
**Host:** `https://sso.ui.com`
**Date:** 2026-11-10

## Summary
`sso.ui.com` reflects the request `Origin` in `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` together with
`Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true` whenever the origin's host ends in `.ui.com`.
This would allow a malicious page hosted on any `*.ui.com` subdomain to make
credentialed cross-origin reads of the victim's SSO API (profile, sessions, MFA list,
addresses, activity). No attacker-controlled `ui.com` subdomain was identified, so
this remains a defense-in-depth / trust-boundary observation rather than a confirmed vuln.

## Reproduction
```
curl -sSi https://sso.ui.com/api/sso/v1/user/self \
  -H 'Origin: https://evil.ui.com' \
  -H "Cookie: UBIC_AUTH=<redacted>"
```
Response includes:
```
access-control-allow-origin: https://evil.ui.com
access-control-allow-credentials: true
vary: origin, Accept-Encoding, Origin
```
Preflight:
```
curl -sSi -X OPTIONS https://sso.ui.com/api/sso/v1/user/self \
  -H 'Origin: https://evil.ui.com' \
  -H 'Access-Control-Request-Method: PUT' \
  -H 'Access-Control-Request-Headers: content-type'
```
allows `PUT, POST, PATCH, DELETE`, `content-type`, `max-age=600`.

## Negative checks
- `Origin: https://evil.com` -> no ACAO.
- `Origin: null` -> no ACAO.
- `Origin: https://account.ui.com.evil.com` -> no ACAO (suffix check is label-based).
- `Origin: https://evil.ubnt.com` -> not tested (out of scope; `ubnt.com` is out of scope).
- `account.svc.ui.com` rejects origins other than `https://account.ui.com` (403).

## Why not confirmed
Exploitation requires the attacker to control content on a `*.ui.com` origin
(user content, uploaded HTML, or a subdomain takeover). Wildcard DNS `*.ui.com` points to
AWS CloudFront and no such controllable origin was found. Without that, the reflected
CORS grants no capability beyond what the victim's own origin already has.
-----PROGRESS-----
# Route Testing Progress — account.ui.com

- Total UI routes discovered: 37
- Fully tested: 9
- Partially tested / blocked: 2
- Pending: 26

Session 2 run: 42843791805, started 2026-11-10T15:24:43Z.

## Fully tested
- `/login` — email + password login works; 2FA required; rate limiting observed (`429 RATE_LIMITED`).
- `/login/mfa` — email OTP (Maildrop) accepted by `POST /api/sso/v1/login/2fa`.
- `/reset-password` — send-reset requires reCAPTCHA (`CHALLENGE_RECAPTCHA_TOKEN_REQUIRED`); anti-bot fields also required. Blocked, no reset email received.
- `/reset-password/password-reset-uuid/:uuid` — confirm is `PUT /api/sso/v1/verify/password/{uuid}` `{password}`; user UUID is NOT the path token (404). Requires emailed reset-request id.
- `/account` — `GET/PUT /api/sso/v1/user/self`; mass-assignment of `role/roles/is_admin/permissions/accounts` ignored; `email` change rejected.
- `/security` — MFA list, sessions, trusted devices, addresses; all cross-account ids protected (404/405/no-op).
- `/requests` — Zendesk ticket list/create; own tickets only.
- `/requests/:ticketId` — cross-account comments return `403 FORBIDDEN`; comment write requires `x-captcha-token`.
- `/login/change-email` — legacy email change is `/user/self` scoped.

## Partially tested / blocked
- `/register` — `POST /api/sso/v2/users` -> `403 CHALLENGE_RECAPTCHA_TOKEN_REQUIRED`.
- `/billing` (+ `/invoices`, `/payments`, `/subscriptions`) — account has no billing customer/orgs; endpoints return `404 Customer not found` / empty `[]`.

## Pending
See `result/inventory/routes.md`. Main untested areas: `/profile`, `/security/suspicious/confirm`,
`/switch`, `/logout`, `/idp/login-result`, `/msp/idp/setup-result`, `/activate`, support forms, backups.

## Candidate issues (not confirmed)
- `sso.ui.com` reflects any `*.ui.com` Origin with `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true`
  (needs an attacker-controlled `*.ui.com` origin to matter). See `result/findings/cors-credentialed-reflection.md`.
