## Work State
### Completed
- Read `skills/AGENT.md`, `skills/client-side-skill.md`, `skills/server-side-skill.md`; preflight done (dirs created, tools present: opencode, curl, git, node/npx, python3, chrome/chromium).
- Appended Session 4 metadata to `result/logs/session.md`.
- Read prior state: `result/SUMMARY.md`, `scope.md`, `progress.md`, `confirmed-vuln.txt`, `inventory/routes.md`, `inventory/endpoints.md`, `testing-inventory.json`, `server-side/account.ui.com/api-inventory.md`.
- Authenticated as Account A end-to-end (email → password → `/login/mfa` email OTP → `/login/trust-device`).
- `/login/trust-device`: `POST https://sso.ui.com/api/sso/v1/user/self/device` body `{"device_id":"<uuid>"}` → `204`; clicking "Trust Device" navigated to `https://account.ui.com/`.
- `/verify`: redirects to `/login` when unauthenticated, to `/` when authenticated (not directly testable).
- `PUT /api/sso/v1/verify/verification-code/{uuid}` → `404` for user uuid, all-zero uuid, and `1` (email-token only; no uuid IDOR).
- `/activate`: client-side `window.location.replace(activate.ui.com)` redirect; not tested.
- Route equivalents confirmed in bundle: `/supportform`, `/mysupport`, `/supportform-umr` → `/requests`; `/supportform-uisp` → external UISP support.
- `/switch`: analyzed `jGt` component — logout + redirect to `/login?login_hint=...`; `redirect` validated by `AC()` → not an arbitrary open redirect.
- `/security/suspicious/confirm`: inspect + confirm APIs use emailed opaque token (`SUSPICIOUS_LOGIN_INSPECT`, POST confirm `{token, decision}`); unguessable, no direct IDOR.
- `/msp/idp/setup-result`: `postMessage` to opener with `targetOrigin = window.location.origin` → safe.
- `/login/change-email` + `/login/change-email/confirm`: legacy endpoints `POST /api/sso/v1/legacy/user/self/email/send {email,password}` and `PUT /api/sso/v1/legacy/user/self/email {email_change_verification_code,email}`; only reachable for accounts in `email_changeable` state (499) — Account A blocked.
- `/backups`: `GET https://cloudaccess.svc.ui.com/api/v1/hosts?withUserData=true...` → empty for test account.
- `POST /api/sso/v1/user/self/2fa/reset` → `404` (path exists only in config, not implemented).
- `GET /api/sso/v1/user/self` → `200` (profile confirmed).
- `GET /api/sso/v1/account-chooser` → `200` `{"accounts":[{"opaque_id":"c576bb0f-cbda-47a8-a243-103c87f9e0cf","username":"testttt12",...}]}`.
- `POST /api/sso/v1/user/self/picture` with JSON body → `415 "application/json not a supported image format"`; profile `picture` remained `null`.

### Active
- Route-by-route testing of remaining pending routes/inventory endpoints; currently probing authenticated `sso.ui.com` APIs via in-page `fetch` (credentials included, CORS reflects `*.ui.com`).
- Picture upload needs retest with an actual image content type (not JSON) to check stored-XSS/SSRF behavior.

### Blocked
- `/reset-password` and `/register`: reCAPTCHA/anti-bot; not bypassed (no brute force per policy).
- `/login/change-email` legacy flow requires account state `email_changeable` (499) — unreachable for Account A.
- `/verify/verification-code/:uuid` requires emailed token; user uuid rejected.
- Billing/subscriptions/backups empty or `404` for test account; limited data surface.
- CORS finding not escalateable without an attacker-controlled `*.ui.com` origin.

## Next Move
1. Retest `POST /api/sso/v1/user/self/picture` with `Content-Type: image/png` (raw PNG bytes and/or SVG) to check stored content-type handling / stored XSS; revert with `picture:null` afterward.
2. Test account-chooser `DELETE /api/sso/v1/account-chooser/{opaque_id}` semantics (IDOR/idempotency) and cross-account behavior using Account B in the isolated context; then continue pending routes (`/login/create-passkey`, `/idp/login-result`, `/security/suspicious/confirm` unauth behavior, `/billing*`, `/subscriptions*`, `/switch`) documenting each in `result/progress.md`, `result/testing-inventory.json`, and `result/inventory/`.

