## Objective
- Autonomously identify valid, reproducible, high-impact vulnerabilities in the authorized `ui.com` scope and report them under `result/`, following `skills/AGENT.md` and the client/server skill files; maintain route-by-route coverage.

## Important Details
- Repo root: `/home/runner/work/aaii-aautomattionn-for-doomainn/aaii-aautomattionn-for-doomainn`
- Scope per `data/targets.txt`: domain `ui.com`; approved components: `ui.com`, `www.ui.com`, `account.ui.com`, `sso.ui.com`, `account.svc.ui.com`, `cloudaccess.svc.ui.com`. Other `*.svc.ui.com`, `*.store.ui.com`, `*.ubnt.com`, etc. are out-of-scope per prior `result/scope.md`.
- `data/targets.txt` includes strict route-by-route testing instructions; operator/Discord webhook handling is recorded in `result/scope.md`; CI reads `result/confirmed-vuln.txt`.
- Prior passive CT enumeration found 1,569 `ui.com` subdomains, dominated by `<uuid>.unifi-hosting[.stg|.dev].ui.com`; prior decision: no DNS brute force/host probing, record out-of-scope.
- Test accounts:
  - A: `tan.tiger5564@maildrop.cc` / `Acd3423@#345`, uuid `d8946fad-2b8e-4cf0-82c5-5d955b57b829`, username `testttt12`
  - B: `overrated.chinchilla337@maildrop.cc` / `Acd3423@#345`, uuid `7c5aab2b-e568-40de-a7a5-ec27df1db94b`, username `test-account-b`
- Auth flow via curl (jars `/tmp/cjA.txt`, `/tmp/cjB.txt`):
  1. `POST https://sso.ui.com/api/sso/v1/login/email` `{"user":"<email>"}`
  2. `POST https://sso.ui.com/api/sso/v1/login` `{"user":"<email>","password":"Acd3423@#345"}` → `499 {"required":"2fa",...}`
  3. Fetch OTP via Maildrop GraphQL: `POST https://api.maildrop.cc/graphql`, mailbox local-part only; regex `verification code is: (\d{6})`.
  4. `POST https://sso.ui.com/api/sso/v1/login/2fa` `{"token":"<otp>"}` → sets `UBIC_AUTH`.
- Always use `curl -c <jar> -b <jar>` together so downgrade/set-cookie changes persist.
- L2 semantics: `GET/DELETE/POST /api/sso/v1/user/self/login/level`; `DELETE` downgrades to 1; `POST /login/level` with password upgrades to 2 (~1800s); `POST /login/level/refresh` at level 1 → `499 L2_REQUIRED`; sensitive ops at level 1 → `499 L2_REQUIRED`. No L2 bypass.
- Browser state: Chrome DevTools MCP works; page 1 is authenticated as A via JS-set `UBIC_AUTH=...` cookie for `.ui.com`; `https://account.ui.com/requests` redirects to `https://account.ui.com/` but account page loads A’s ticket. `grecaptcha.enterprise` was injected/loaded on page.
- Captcha: site key `RECAPTCHA_ACCOUNT_BACKEND_SITE_KEY_ID` = `6LfyUkwpAAAAAJ6-mN1q_IAe0bM8pit_lxc0anmv`; script `https://www.google.com/recaptcha/enterprise.js`; action enum includes `ZENDESK_CREATE_TICKET_COMMENT` and `submit`.
- Zendesk ticket create body from bundle `Jet` component: `{"ticket_form_id":31131542026135,"requester":{"email":...,"name":...},"tags":[...],"subject":...,"comment":{"body":...},"custom_fields":[{"id":31131569689239,"value":...}]}`. Server appears to ignore `requester` and use session user.
- Zendesk ownership: A Zendesk id `44644434942359`, external_id A uuid; B Zendesk id `44644404389911`, external_id B uuid. B owns closed ticket `6133375`; A owns closed ticket `6136591`.
- Ticket creation rate limit is per-account and persists several minutes: A succeeded at 14:12:50 then `429` at 14:15:12; B was `429` earlier. Pace requests.
- Credentialed CORS on `sso.ui.com` reflects `*.ui.com` origins, but exploitation requires attacker-controlled content on some `*.ui.com` origin; none found. `secure-uploads.ui.com`, `images.svc.ui.com`, `account-cdn.svc.ui.com`, and `unifi-hosting` are out-of-scope/not approved for active testing.
- Session 6: run `43034033571`, start `2026-11-11T14:02:45Z`, decision `preserved`.

## Work State

### Completed
- Preflight, read `skills/AGENT.md`, client/server skills, prior `result/` state; Session 6 logged in `result/logs/session.md`; both A/B authenticated.
- Prior low/info findings re-verified; `result/confirmed-vuln.txt` still has no confirmed high-impact.
- Account chooser: `GET https://sso.ui.com/api/sso/v1/account-chooser` for A, B, and unauthenticated all return `{"accounts":[]}`; `OPTIONS` 200. Saved accounts are client-side / no server-side IDOR. Deprioritized.
- Trusted devices/sessions IDOR: A `DELETE /user/self/sessions/<B-session>` → `404 {"detail":"No SessionMetadata matches the given query.","error":"ERROR"}`; A `DELETE /user/self/trusted_devices?id=<B-device>` → `204` but B’s list unchanged, so no-op. `POST /user/self/device` with `{device_id,user:B,uuid:B}` → `400 {"detail":"No device information found.","error":"DEVICE_INFO_NOT_FOUND"}`; requires device cookie. Test device cleanup delete → `204`.
- Settings mass assignment: `GET/PATCH /api/sso/v1/user/self/settings`; empty PATCH 200; body with `passwordless:true,twofa_enabled:false,is_verified:false,role:admin,roles:[admin],accounts:{...}` → 200 unchanged. Profile remains `twofa_enabled:true`, `is_verified:true`, `roles:null`.
- Zendesk cross-account:
  - B create ticket with `requester` A → `429 RATE_LIMITED`.
  - A create ticket with `requester` B at 14:12:50 → `201`, ticket `6136591`, but `requester_id` `44644434942359` (A), not B’s `44644404389911`; requester spoof ignored.
  - A’s open list had `6136591`; B’s open list empty; B `GET /zendesk/comments/6136591` → `403 FORBIDDEN`.
  - A `PUT /zendesk/ticket/6136591/close` → 200 closed; cleanup verified in A closed list.
  - B ticket `6133375`: B `GET /zendesk/comments/6133375` (path style) → 200 with full ticket/comments/`html_body`; A same → `403 FORBIDDEN`; A `PUT /zendesk/ticket/6133375/close` → `403`; A `GET /zendesk/ticket/6133375` → 404. Query style `?ticket_id=` returns 404 for both; path style is correct.
- Zendesk user params ignored: `GET /zendesk/user?email=...`, `?requester_id=...`, `?user_id=...`, `?id=...`, `?uuid=...` all return A’s own Zendesk user.
- `POST /user/self/zendesk_user` with `{"external_id":B_uuid}` → `404 {"message":"Not found"}`; external_id unchanged. Prior full-body mass assignment returned 200 but ignored.
- reCAPTCHA: browser-generated enterprise tokens (actions `ZENDESK_CREATE_TICKET_COMMENT`, `submit`, lengths ~2446–2510) sent via `x-captcha-token` to `POST /zendesk/search_tickets` and `POST /zendesk/comment/6136591` all → `403 {"code":"FORBIDDEN","message":"Did not pass reCAPTCHA validation"}`. Header spoof attempts `CF-IPCountry: CN`, `CloudFront-Viewer-Country: CN`, `X-Country-Code: CN`, `X-Forwarded-For: 114.114.114.114` still → `400 {"code":"BAD_REQUEST","message":"Invalid input, reCAPTCHA token was not provided"}`. No China-skip bypass.
- `/api/sso/v1/user/self/2fa/reset`: GET and POST (no body and `{}`) → 404 Not Found; endpoint not implemented; B MFA unchanged.
- IdP result flow: `FRt` reads `code`/`state`, calls `completeIdpLogin`, then `window.location.replace(next)`; `X5` error component only logs `description` to telemetry, does not render it. `POST /api/sso/v1/idp/login-result` with arbitrary code/state (`https://evil.com/`, `/account`, empty) → `400 {"error":"STATE_MISSING","detail":"Login state missing or malformed."}`.
- Chat JWT: `GET /chat/messaging/jwt` → 404; `POST` with A session → 200 HS256 JWT `{external_id:A_uuid,email:A_email,email_verified:true,scope:"user",name:"OpenCodeTest"}`; body/query overrides ignored.
- Profile mass assignment/address IDOR/roles beta retested and protected as previously recorded; cleaned up test addresses/roles.
- Observed client JS secrets: Google Maps key `AIzaSyBE3JpOF9gNSsb83dpZKLUqFkmBAsPr0-w`, reCAPTCHA site keys, SendSafely/IRONCLAD identifiers — third-party/low, not confirmed high-impact.

### Active
- Inspecting bundle for `/user/self/device` and trust-device call sites (`device_id`, `device_name`, `device_model`, `session`, device fingerprint cookie) to see if full client-supplied device info can bypass `DEVICE_INFO_NOT_FOUND` or mass-assign `user`; last grep output was truncated and saved to `/home/runner/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/tool_1caf98836001i64wZIwn0kzrnu`.
- Evaluating CORS chain feasibility: only exploitable if attacker can host HTML/JS on a `*.ui.com` origin; candidate image/CDN/hosting subdomains are out-of-scope or serve fixed/non-executable content.
- Considering passkey registration/login with a virtual authenticator; add-passkey uses `Y2.webAuthnChallenge`/`/mfa/webauthn/options`, but no existing keys and MCP does not expose WebAuthn virtual authenticator.
- Considering Zendesk CC/collaborator injection and `html_body` sanitization after rate limit; `html-react-parser` rendering likely prevents script execution, so self-XSS value is low.
- Remaining pending routes to test: `/login/change-email/confirm` (check B `email_changeable`), `/supportform`, `/supportform-uisp`, `/supportform-umr`, `/mysupport`, `/backups`, `/billing/*`, `/subscriptions/*`, `/activate`.

### Blocked
- Zendesk ticket creation `429 RATE_LIMITED` on `account.svc.ui.com`; must wait/pacing.
- Zendesk search/comment captcha validation rejects browser-generated tokens `403 "Did not pass reCAPTCHA validation"`; header spoofing does not bypass.
- `/2fa/reset` not implemented (`404`).
- IdP login result requires valid `state`; no IdP configured/testable, state format unknown.
- `/login/create-passkey` blocked: no registered keys; `/mfa/webauthn/options` → 404 `User or verified keys not found`; virtual authenticator unavailable.
- Device trust creation blocked by missing device info/cookie.
- Registration and password reset require reCAPTCHA.
- `/login/change-email/confirm` blocked for A by `email_changeable`/499; B eligibility not yet checked.
- Billing/enterprise org IDOR not testable without real customer/org identifiers.
- Account deletion not tested (risk/no safe throwaway account); out-of-scope services not probed.

## Next Move
1. Finish bundle inspection of `/user/self/device` / trust-device call sites to derive the exact device fingerprint payload/cookie; if client-controlled `device_info`/`user` fields exist, test cross-account trust injection, otherwise record the negative and move on.
2. Test B’s `/login/change-email/confirm` eligibility and then work through remaining reachable pending routes one-by-one (`/supportform*`, `/mysupport`, `/backups`, `/activate`, `/billing/*`, `/subscriptions/*`), documenting each.
3. After >10 minutes without `account.svc` writes, single Zendesk ticket create to test `collaborator_ids`/`email_ccs` injection and `html_body` sanitization; do not spam due to per-account rate limit.

