# Scope

## Target entries (from `data/targets.txt`)
- Domain-only target: `ui.com`
- Operator note references account subdomain: `https://account.ui.com/login`
- Credentials available for `https://account.ui.com/login` (Test Account A and B).

## Classification
- Domain-only target: `ui.com` and its explicitly approved components (same-origin
  hosts discovered within the ui.com domain, e.g. `www.ui.com`, `account.ui.com`).
- No URL list provided.

## User Instructions (restated)
- Discover all interesting and unique UI routes and API endpoints on the target.
- Visit each UI route one-by-one with Chrome MCP; wait 5-10s for JS to load.
- Test both client-side and server-side bugs per route, completing one route fully
  (test + document) before moving to the next.
- Maintain a progress report: total routes, fully tested, pending, which are done.
- Before testing each route, read client-side and server-side skill files and
  follow them exactly.
- Per-route report: client-side findings, server-side findings, route completion status.
- Create two test accounts on the target subdomain and save credentials for
  testing; if account creation is not possible, test unauthenticated endpoints only.
- Do not ask questions; make reasonable decisions.
- Final goal: identify valid, impactful, reportable vulnerabilities.
- If a confirmed vuln is found, send a Discord notification to the provided webhook.

## Authorization source / assumptions
- Authorization is asserted by the repository's `data/` scope. Only assets under
  the `ui.com` domain that are explicitly part of the target are tested.
- Test accounts in `creds/test-account.txt` are disposable/public test accounts.

## In-scope components
- `ui.com` (apex, redirects to www)
- `www.ui.com`
- `account.ui.com` (login/account flows; explicitly referenced in operator note and creds)

## Out-of-scope components
- Any third-party origin, CDN, partner, acquisition, or unrelated subdomain not
  explicitly listed. Discovered out-of-scope assets are recorded in
  `result/out-of-scope.txt`.

## Program restrictions
- No destructive/disruptive testing, no DoS/load/stress, no brute force, no mass
  fuzzing, no real-user data access, no social engineering.
- Use only test-owned data/accounts; harmless payloads.
- Respect rate limits and program policy; stricter rule wins.

## Session 5 scope notes
- Added `https://www.ui.com/` client-side review (already listed as in-scope component).
- Performed passive certificate-transparency enumeration of `ui.com` only; no DNS
  brute force and no probing of unrelated subdomains was performed.
- `*.svc.ui.com` services other than `account.svc.ui.com` / `cloudaccess.svc.ui.com`,
  `store.ui.com`, and non-`ui.com` domains remain out of scope and are recorded in
  `result/out-of-scope.txt`. No scope expansion was performed.
===
# Out-of-scope assets observed (not tested)

This file records assets discovered during in-scope testing that were NOT tested, per
AGENT.md §2/§6. Scope is the ui.com domain and its explicitly approved components
(ui.com, www.ui.com, account.ui.com, sso.ui.com, account.svc.ui.com,
cloudaccess.svc.ui.com). Everything below is either a different registrable domain or a
third-party service.

## Third-party origins loaded by www.ui.com / account.ui.com
- cdn.cookielaw.org, geolocation.onetrust.com (OneTrust consent)
- www.googletagmanager.com, www.google-analytics.com (GTM/GA)
- static.hotjar.com (Hotjar)
- dev.visualwebsiteoptimizer.com (VWO)
- www.redditstatic.com, pixel-config.reddit.com, alb.reddit.com (Reddit pixel)
- js.stripe.com, m.stripe.network (Stripe)
- static.ada.support (Ada chat)
- images.svc.ui.com (image CDN; only static images requested)

## Other ui.com infrastructure (not in the approved component list)
- `*.svc.ui.com` services other than account.svc/cloudaccess.svc, e.g.
  fabric.svc, billing.svc, enterprise.svc, lte-api.svc, u5g-api.svc, megaphone.svc,
  geo.svc, images.svc, direct.svc, feedback.svc, account-cdn.svc
- `*.store.ui.com` / `store.ui.com` (Shopify storefront; separate commerce system)
- `*.ubnt.com`, `uisp.com`, `amplifi.com`, `unifi.com` and other non-ui.com domains
- 1,569 `ui.com` subdomains from certificate-transparency enumeration, dominated by
  `<uuid>.unifi-hosting[.stg|.dev].ui.com`. Passive enumeration only; no DNS brute force
  or host probing was performed (would be broad/out-of-scope and risk disruptive testing).

## Notes
- The existing `sso.ui.com` credentialed-CORS observation would only become exploitable
  if an attacker could control content on some `*.ui.com` origin. No such origin was
  found; wildcard `*.ui.com` serves a fixed SPA. See
  `result/findings/cors-credentialed-reflection.md`.
