## Objective
- Autonomously identify valid, reproducible, high-impact vulnerabilities in the authorized `ui.com` scope and report them under `result/`, following `skills/AGENT.md` and the client/server skill files; maintain route-by-route coverage.

## Important Details
- Repo root: `/home/runner/work/aaii-aautomattionn-for-doomainn/aaii-aautomattionn-for-doomainn`
- Scope per `data/targets.txt`: domain `ui.com`; approved components: `ui.com`, `www.ui.com`, `account.ui.com`, `sso.ui.com`, `account.svc.ui.com`, `cloudaccess.svc.ui.com`. Other `*.svc.ui.com`, `*.store.ui.com`, `*.ubnt.com`, etc. are out-of-scope per prior `result/scope.md`.
- `result/scope.md` lists only `ui.com`, `www.ui.com`, `account.ui.com` as in-scope components while also referencing prior approval of `sso.ui.com`/`account.svc.ui.com`; avoid expanding beyond previously tested assets.
- `data/targets.txt` includes strict route-by-route testing instructions; operator/Discord webhook handling is recorded in `result/scope.md`; CI reads `result/confirmed-vuln.txt`.
- Prior passive CT enumeration found 1,569 `ui.com` subdomains, dominated by `<uuid>.unifi-hosting[.stg|.dev].ui.com`; prior decision: no DNS brute force/host probing, record out-of-scope.
- Test accounts:
  - A: `tan.tiger5564@maildrop.cc` / `Acd3423@#345`, uuid `d8946fad-2b8e-4cf0-82c5-5d955b57b829`, username `testttt12`
  - B: `overrated.chinchilla337@maildrop.cc` / `Acd3423@#345`, uuid `7c5aab2b-e568-40de-a7a5-ec27df1db94b`, username `test-account-b`
- Auth flow via curl (jars `/tmp/cjA.txt`, `/tmp/cjB.txt`, fresh A jar `/tmp/cjA_dev.txt`):
  1. `POST https://sso.ui.com/api/sso/v1/login/email` `{"user":"<email>"}` — does not trigger OTP.
  2. `POST https://sso.ui.com/api/sso/v1/login` `{"user":"<email>","password":"Acd3423@#345"}` → `499 {"required":"2fa",...}`, `set-cookie: UBIC_2FA=...`.
  3. Fetch OTP via Maildrop GraphQL: `POST https://api.maildrop.cc/graphql`. Schema changed: old `mailbox` field is invalid (`Cannot query field "mailbox" on type "Query". Did you mean "inbox"?`). Use `query { inbox(mailbox:"<local-part>") { id headerfrom subject date } }` and `query { message(mailbox:"<local-part>", id:"<id>") { id subject data html } }`. Message fields are `id ip helo date mailfrom rcptto headerfrom subject data html`; there is **no `text` field**. Regex `verification code is:\s*(\d{6})` still works.
  4. `POST https://sso.ui.com/api/sso/v1/login/2fa` `{"token":"<otp>"}` → clears `UBIC_2FA`, sets `UBIC_AUTH`.
- Always use `curl -c <jar> -b <jar>` together so set-cookie changes persist. `grep -v '^#'` hides HttpOnly jar entries (`#HttpOnly_.ui.com`), so do not use it to verify cookies.
- Login responses set only `UBIC_2FA` then `UBIC_AUTH`; no `UBIC_DEVICE` cookie. `GET /api/sso/v1/user/self/device` refreshes `UBIC_AUTH` but returns `404` with empty body even with a browser User-Agent/Origin/Referer and a valid session.
- L2 semantics: `GET/DELETE/POST /api/sso/v1/user/self/login/level`; `DELETE` downgrades to 1; `POST /login/level` with password upgrades to 2 (~1800s); `POST /login/level/refresh` at level 1 → `499 L2_REQUIRED`; sensitive ops at level 1 → `499 L2_REQUIRED`. No L2 bypass. Fresh A session at 14:21:27 has `L2:1794407487` (~valid until 14:51 UTC).
- Browser state: Chrome DevTools MCP works; page 1 is authenticated as A via JS-set HttpOnly `UBIC_AUTH` (not visible in `document.cookie`); `https://account.ui.com/requests` redirects to `https://account.ui.com/` but account page loads A’s ticket. `GET https://sso.ui.com/api/sso/v1/user/self` from the page returns 200; `GET .../device` returns 404 there too.
- Captcha: site key `RECAPTCHA_ACCOUNT_BACKEND_SITE_KEY_ID` = `6LfyUkwpAAAAAJ6-mN1q_IAe0bM8pit_lxc0anmv`; script `https://www.google.com/recaptcha/enterprise.js`; action enum includes `ZENDESK_CREATE_TICKET_COMMENT` and `submit`.
- Zendesk API paths on `account.svc.ui.com`: `/zendesk/user`, `/zendesk/ticket`, `/zendesk/tickets`, `/zendesk/tickets/closed`, `/zendesk/tickets/ccd`, `/zendesk/search_tickets`, `/zendesk/search_ccd`, `/zendesk/comments/<id>`, `/zendesk/comment`, `/zendesk/ticket/{ticketId}/close`, `/chat/messaging/jwt`.
- Zendesk ticket create body: `{"ticket_form_id":31131542026135,"requester":{"email":...,"name":...},"tags":[...],"subject":...,"comment":{"body":...},"custom_fields":[{"id":31131569689239,"value":...}]}`. Server ignores `requester` and uses session user.
- Zendesk ownership: A Zendesk id `44644434942359`; B Zendesk id `44644404389911`; A ticket `6136591`; B ticket `6133375`. Path-style comments endpoint works; query style `?ticket_id=` returns 404.
- Zendesk ticket creation rate limit: per-account, `x-ratelimit-limit: 1`, `x-ratelimit-remaining: 0`. B at 14:22:33 → `429 {"code":"RATE_LIMITED","message":"You've exceeded the allowed request rate limit. Please try again later"}`, `x-ratelimit-reset: 1794410373` (~15:19 UTC). A’s last successful create was 14:12:50, so A likely resets ~15:12 UTC.
- Credentialed CORS on `sso.ui.com` reflects `*.ui.com` origins, but exploitation requires attacker-controlled content on some `*.ui.com` origin; none found. `secure-uploads.ui.com`, `images.svc.ui.com`, `account-cdn.svc.ui.com`, and `unifi-hosting` are out-of-scope/not approved for active testing.
- Bundle facts:
  - Device API class `b4`: `getAll` → `/api/sso/v1/user/self/trusted_devices`; `getDeviceData` → `/api/sso/v1/user/self/device`; `create = async e => hC(new URL(y4.paths.device, J$.ssoBase).href, {device_id: e.device_id})`; `deleteMany` appends `?id=` per id.
  - Hook `x4` uses query key `V.TRUSTED_DEVICE`; route constant `j8e='/login/trust-device'`.
  - Special-routes set `Hpe` includes `/login/trust-device`, `/security/suspicious/confirm`, `/login/create-passkey`, and `Lpe.switch`.
  - Open-redirect validator `AC()` only allows registrable domains `['ubnt.com','ui.com','uisp.com']` over http/https.
  - Passkey login calls `e.login({publicKeyCredential, remember_me})`; login body otherwise has no device fields.
  - `setupLoginToken: /api/sso/v1/user/self/token/setup`, `approveLoginToken: /api/sso/v1/user/self/token/login` are present and untested; potential login-token/QR cross-account approval IDOR.
- `result/testing-inventory.json` has 38 routes; `result/progress.md` says 37 total (21 fully tested, 10 partial, 6 blocked). Route `5` (`/login/trust-device`) is marked done with note “POST /user/self/device {device_id} -> 204; trusted-session TTL 31536000s”, but this was likely from a real-browser device-cookie session in Session 4; current curl sessions cannot reproduce it.

